From 5b79f7518d84e56cc1327b33bd8cbc066b722c1c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tomaszstaniak <nbw.designs@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 14:55:55 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 6/9] runtime: 40-bit heap, non-nil env, and an exit that reaps
 parked Ms

Three fixes found by running the binary on the patched kernel, each the
next fatal error the one before it revealed -- which is what a working
write1 buys: the runtime names its own next problem.

- Page allocator. At 48 heapAddrBits the page summaries reserve ~585 MB,
  fine when reservation is lazy mmap but not when the heap is one
  AllocMem arena, where a reservation costs real memory. AROS joins
  ios/arm64 at 40 bits (~2.3 MB of summaries) and drops the amd64
  sign-extension arenaBaseOffset with it. "failed to reserve page
  summary memory" -> past mallocinit.

- goenvs left envs nil; gogetenv reads nil as "before env init" and
  throws. Make it an empty non-nil slice. "getenv before env init" ->
  past schedinit.

- exit. libpthread's ADD2EXIT hook pthread_joins every thread before the
  process may end (so code isn't unloaded under a running thread). A Go M
  parked in semasleep never returns, so a plain exit() hangs -- this is
  in the AROS source, not guessed. So exit now flags the process exiting
  and broadcasts every per-M semaphore; each parked M, waking in
  x_cgo_aros_semasleep, leaves through pthread_exit instead of returning
  to Go, and the hook then finds nothing to wait for.

The runtime now starts, allocates, runs the scheduler and spawns the GC
goroutines. It still hits a fatal error late in bringup, not yet pinned.

